 Prefix Sums  ·  USACO Guide · Silver
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  ## Introduction

  Given an array a[1], a[2], …, a[N], a prefix sum array stores pₖ = ∑ᵢ₌₁ᵏ aᵢ
  for every k, with p₀ = 0. Any range sum is then a difference of two prefix
  sums:

  aₗ + aₗ₊₁ + ⋯ + aᵣ = pᵣ - pₗ₋₁

  Building p takes O(N) and each query O(1), so Q queries cost O(N + Q)
  instead of O(NQ).

